menu "Example Configuration"

    config THERMOSTAT_CONTROLLER_SUBSCRIBE_MIN_INTERVAL
        int "Minimum subscription interval (s)"
        default 1
        range 0 60
        help
            Minimum interval, in seconds, requested when subscribing to the bound thermostat's
            ThermostatRunningState attribute.

    config THERMOSTAT_CONTROLLER_SUBSCRIBE_MAX_INTERVAL
        int "Maximum subscription interval (s)"
        default 10
        range 1 3600
        help
            Maximum interval, in seconds, requested when subscribing to the bound thermostat's
            ThermostatRunningState attribute. This bounds how quickly a heat demand change is
            reported when no attribute report is otherwise received (keep-alive).

    config THERMOSTAT_CONTROLLER_HEATING_HYSTERESIS_CENTIDEGREES
        int "LocalTemperature/OccupiedHeatingSetpoint fallback hysteresis (0.01 degC)"
        default 50
        range 0 500
        help
            Some thermostats do not report ThermostatRunningState, or report it without the
            Heat bit changing. As a fallback, heat demand is also inferred by comparing
            LocalTemperature to OccupiedHeatingSetpoint: demand turns on once LocalTemperature
            drops to (setpoint - hysteresis) or below, and turns off once LocalTemperature
            reaches the setpoint. This avoids rapid toggling around the setpoint. Value is in
            hundredths of a degree Celsius, matching the Matter attribute encoding (default 50
            = 0.5 degC).

endmenu
